<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guna people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kuna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Guna, formerly spelled Kuna, are an indigenous people of Panama and north-western Colombia, living mainly on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guna-yala">San Blas</a> islands and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast of Darién. During the Scottish Darien scheme of 1698–1700 they were friendly to the colonists, who hoped for their help against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. In 1925 they rose in the Tule Revolution, which led to their autonomy in the comarca of Guna Yala.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guna-people.jpg" alt="Guna people" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imakjak · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kunawoman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
